      "name": "Spoilage or loss of units",
      "why_safe": "No evidence of spoilage or loss. The collection rate is 'usable units', implying quality control. Excluding loss is safe because any loss would reduce the answer, but the question asks for received units; if loss occurs, the answer would be lower, but we have no evidence to quantify it. However, the resolution note says 'the number of units the hospital actually holds' \u2013 if units are lost after receipt, that would affect holdings. But no evidence of such loss. We assume no loss."
    }
